\":584},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":992,\"outputTokens\":17,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001077,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000,\"canonicalModel\":\"claude-haiku-4-5\",\"provider\":\"firstParty\"},\"claude-sonnet-5\":{\"inputTokens\":50,\"outputTokens\":8980,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1103388,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":36494,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.6848304000000001,\"contextWindow\":1000000,\"maxOutputTokens\":64000,\"canonicalModel\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"provider\":\"firstParty\"}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"fast_mode_disabled_reason\":\"sdk_opt_in_required\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"api_error_status\":null,\"result\":\"Only `internal/cli/export.go` changed, `go.mod`/`go.sum` untouched, and no changes were committed.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFound the regression in `checkpointBranchDestinations.BranchesFor` (`internal/cli/export.go:1478`). It checked the checkpoint's recorded metadata branch *before* checking default-branch reachability, so once a feature branch merged, its checkpoints still filed under the old feature-branch folder instead of moving to the default branch.\\n\\n**Fix:** reordered the check to test default-branch reachability (`DefaultCheckpointIDs`) first, falling back to the metadata branch only when the checkpoint isn't reachable from the default branch \u2014 matching the intended behavior recorded in project history (\\\"a session log lands in `sessions/main/` when its checkpoint ID appears in commits reachable from the default branch... the manifest preserves [the original branch] as `source_branch`\\\"). The `SourceBranch` field, which remembers where the session originally came from, was already being set independently and needed no change.\\n\\n**Validation:**\\n- `go build ./...` \u2014 passed\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/... -run 'Export|Branch|Snapshot' -v` \u2014 all passed\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/...` (full package) \u2014 passed\",\"ttft_ms\":1901,\"ttft_stream_ms\":809,\"time_to_request_ms\":11,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":284962,\"uuid\":\"3a33df23-86fa-4324-8866-1614324b2945\"}\n",
